HOW TO MAKE WAR OBSOLETE
Source: 𝙼𝚒𝚔𝚎 🜎 @OhWellMike

TYPE: Peace-system framework
GOAL: Make war unnecessary, unprofitable, and illegitimate
      so it becomes more like dueling than politics.

CORE VARIABLES
  V1  Security without vetoed atrocity
  V2  Inclusive rule-of-law governance
  V3  Economic incentives away from arms
  V4  Permanent prevention infrastructure
  V5  Cultural norms against dehumanization
  V6  Trauma repair and revenge-cycle break
  V7  Binding rules on emerging weapons

FUNDAMENTALS
  Mutual, verified disarmament only
  Leader accountability, not population punishment
  Nonviolent options and self-defense remain possible
  No imposed world government by force
  Aggression treated as a crime under accountable institutions

01  SECURITY WITHOUT WAR
    Reform UN Security Council so mass atrocities cannot be vetoed.
    Strengthen regional peacekeeping.
    Arms control must be verifiable and reciprocal.

02  GOVERNANCE THAT INCLUDES EVERYONE
    Rule of law.
    Minority rights.
    Autonomy or federalism where needed.
    Anti-corruption.
    Real democratic accountability.

03  ECONOMIC INCENTIVES FOR PEACE
    Shift military spending to health, education, climate.
    Cut arms sales to abusers.
    Resource transparency.
    Convert defense industries to civilian production.

04  PERMANENT PREVENTION INFRASTRUCTURE
    Fund early warning, mediators, local peacebuilders, civilian protection.
    Include women and young people in peace processes.
    Targeted sanctions on leaders and war profiteers, not whole populations.

05  CHANGE THE CULTURE
    Teach critical thinking, media literacy, empathy across borders.
    Challenge dehumanizing propaganda.
    Confront painful histories honestly.
    Make cheering for war shameful.
    Make peacemaking prestigious.

06  HEAL TRAUMA AND BREAK REVENGE CYCLES
    Fund mental health, truth commissions, reparations, fighter reintegration.
    Hold perpetrators accountable while helping societies stop reliving the same wound.

07  GOVERN NEW TECHNOLOGIES
    Global rules for cyberwar, drones, and autonomous weapons.
    Use satellites and AI for verification and early warning, not arms-race escalation.

FINAL LEVER: INCENTIVES
    Leaders who start wars lose power.
    Peacebuilders gain status and resources.
    Remove elite profit and ordinary fear of defenselessness.

OUTPUT STATE
    War becomes harder to start and eventually unthinkable.
